      "writtenOn": "2025-09-03T08:58:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003eThis is a limitation of GraphicsTracker, currently.\n\u003e(And it should be addressed and aligned to Graphics system.)\n\nYes, I think so. Could please you let me try to impl GraphicsTracker\nsupport unlimited slot with flag(`WB_UNLIMITED_SLOTS`)?\n\n\u003e However you cannot set maxDequeue over the current limit.\n\u003e So crashing by CHECK() does not happen.\n\nYes, It\u0027s designed the max support is maxDequeue.\nBut CCodecBufferChannel supports HAL codec update `outputDelay` here: media/codec2/sfplugin/CCodecBufferChannel.cpp:2538\n\nA new maxDequeueCount would be calcuated based on the `outputDelay`\nand set it to BufferQueueProducer via `output-\u003esurface-\u003esetMaxDequeuedBufferCount`: media/codec2/sfplugin/CCodecBufferChannel.cpp:2364\n\nIf the HAL codec update a `outputDelay` which is greater than the maxDequeue,\nAnd there is no valid-check, it would be setted to BufferQueueProducer which is\nsupported unlimited slots.\n\nNext, it\u0027s possible get a slot which is greater than max from BufferQueueProducer.\n\nThere is a issue:431710660 in our devices, the hal codec has some post-process which update delay then max.\n\n\u003e What do you want to achieve with this CL?\n\nThis CL add valid-check to avoid to extend BufferQueueProducer slot count which is greater than max.",
      "parentUuid": "218fa2b1_1a7aa397",
      "revId": "0f1c2315883248d9d7d4e434f2d3afb7a54c0fcd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
